<article class="env-lemma" id="02H5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02H5">Lemma <span data-tag="02H5">37.9.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(a, a') : (X \subset X') \to (Y \subset Y')$ be a morphism of first order thickenings over $S$. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \theta : a^*\Omega _{Y/S} \to \mathcal{C}_{X/X'}  \]
</div>
  <p> be an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-linear map. Then there exists a unique morphism of pairs $(b, b') : (X \subset X') \to (Y \subset Y')$ such that (1) and (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/04FG" data-tag="04FG">37.9.1</a> hold and the derivation $D$ and $\theta $ are related by Equation (<a href="/tag/04BV" data-tag="04BV">37.9.1.1</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We simply set $b = a$ and we define $(b')^\sharp $ to be the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (a')^\sharp + D : a^{-1}\mathcal{O}_{Y'} \to \mathcal{O}_{X'}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $D$ is as in Equation (<a href="/tag/04BV" data-tag="04BV">37.9.1.1</a>). We omit the verification that $(b')^\sharp $ is a map of sheaves of $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebras and that (1) and (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/04FG" data-tag="04FG">37.9.1</a> hold. Equation (<a href="/tag/04BV" data-tag="04BV">37.9.1.1</a>) holds by construction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>